{"name":"Antiquity","hex":"#c1a87c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Antiquity","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The period of Ancient Greece and Ancient Rome."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Antiquity"}],"entries":[{"title":"Antiquities","blocks":[{"text":"Antiquities are objects from antiquity, especially the civilizations of the Mediterranean such as the Classical antiquity of Greece and Rome, Ancient Egypt, and the other Ancient Near Eastern cultures such as Ancient Persia (Iran). Artifacts from earlier periods such as the Mesolithic, and other civilizations from Asia and elsewhere may also be covered by the term. The phenomenon of giving a high value to ancient artifacts is found in other cultures, notably China, where Chinese ritual bronzes, three to two thousand years old, have been avidly collected and imitated for centuries, and the Pre-Columbian cultures of Mesoamerica, where in particular the artifacts of the earliest Olmec civilization are found reburied in significant sites of later cultures up to the Spanish Conquest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/The_Parthenon_sculptures%2C_British_Museum_%2814063376069%29_%282%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-The_Parthenon_sculptures%2C_British_Museum_%2814063376069%29_%282%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antiquities","wikidata":"Q2906114"},{"title":"Ancient history","blocks":[{"text":"Ancient history is a time period from the beginning of writing and recorded human history through late antiquity. The span of recorded history is roughly 5,000 years, beginning with the development of Sumerian cuneiform script. Ancient history covers all continents inhabited by humans in the period 3000 BC – AD 500."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Denis_Bourez_-_British_Museum%2C_London_%288747049029%29_%282%29.jpg/330px-Denis_Bourez_-_British_Museum%2C_London_%288747049029%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_history","wikidata":"Q41493"},{"title":"Antiquity (journal)","blocks":[{"text":"Antiquity is a bimonthly peer-reviewed academic journal covering archaeology worldwide from all periods. The editor-in-chief is Robin Skeates. Since 2015, the journal has been published by Cambridge University Press."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7d/Antiquity_Volume_1_cover.jpg/330px-Antiquity_Volume_1_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antiquity_(journal)","wikidata":"Q4775205"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Human_headed_winged_bull_facing.jpg/500px-Human_headed_winged_bull_facing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Human_headed_winged_bull_facing.jpg/1280px-Human_headed_winged_bull_facing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Human_headed_winged_bull_facing.jpg/500px-Human_headed_winged_bull_facing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Assyrian lamassu in the Louvre","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHuman_headed_winged_bull_facing.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Chinese_ritual_wine_server_%28guang%29.jpg/500px-Chinese_ritual_wine_server_%28guang%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Chinese_ritual_wine_server_%28guang%29.jpg/1280px-Chinese_ritual_wine_server_%28guang%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 